    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q12",
      "question": "<p>In this question you should show all stages of your working.</p><p>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p>(i) Solve, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0 &lt; \\theta \\leq 450^\\circ\"></span>, the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5 \\cos^2 \\theta = 6 \\sin \\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving your answers to one decimal place.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>(ii) (a) A student’s attempt to solve the question</p><p>“Solve, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-90^\\circ &lt; x &lt; 90^\\circ\"></span>, the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3 \\tan x - 5 \\sin x = 0\"></span>”</p><p>is set out below.</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3 \\tan x - 5 \\sin x = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3 \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} - 5 \\sin x = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3 \\sin x - 5 \\sin x \\cos x = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3 - 5 \\cos x = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos x = \\frac{3}{5}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x = 53.1^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Identify two errors or omissions made by this student, giving a brief explanation of each.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The first four positive solutions, in order of size, of the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos(5\\alpha + 40^\\circ) = \\frac{3}{5}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha_1, \\alpha_2, \\alpha_3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha_4\"></span></p><p>(b) Find, to the nearest degree, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha_4\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
