    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q13",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:82mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q13-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Linear plot of log heart rate against log mass.\"></figure><p>The resting heart rate, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\"></span>, of a mammal, measured in beats per minute, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h = pm^q\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are constants and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> is the mass of the mammal measured in kg.</p><p>Figure 2 illustrates the linear relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10} h\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10} m\"></span>.</p><p>The line meets the vertical <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10} h\"></span> axis at 2.25 and has a gradient of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-0.235\"></span></p><p>(a) Find, to 3 significant figures, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>A particular mammal has a mass of 5 kg and a resting heart rate of 119 beats per minute.</p><p>(b) Comment on the suitability of the model for this mammal.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(c) With reference to the model, interpret the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
