      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q14",
      "question": "<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x)\"></span> where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x) = -3x^2 + 12x + 8\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(a) Write <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span> in the form</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a(x + b)^2 + c\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a, b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has a maximum turning point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span>.</p><p>(b) Find the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:104mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q14-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Parabola with maximum M and shaded region R.\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> passes through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span> and is parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis.</p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 3, is bounded by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C, l\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis.</p><p>(c) Using algebraic integration, find the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
