      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q15",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:113mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q15-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4. Circle with centre N and tangent at P.\"></figure><p>Figure 4 shows a sketch of a circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with centre <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N(7, 4)\"></span></p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{3}x\"></span> is a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p>Find</p><p>(a) the equation of line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PN\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = mx + c\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) an equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>The line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{3}x + k\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a non-zero constant, is also a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p>(c) Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
