      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2021-november/q16",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x)\"></span> where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x) = ax^3 + 15x^2 - 39x + b\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants.</p><p>Given</p><ul><li>the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2, 10)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>the gradient of the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2, 10)\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-3\"></span></li></ul><p>(a) (i) show that the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\"></span></p><p>(ii) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has no stationary points.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(c) Write <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x - 4)Q(x)\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q(x)\"></span> is a quadratic expression to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(d) Hence deduce the coordinates of the points of intersection of the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = f(0.2x)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>and the coordinate axes.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
